---
// src/components/Careers/RoleOverview.astro
---

<section class="relative w-full bg-[#f4ede0] py-14 sm:py-20 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 border-b border-[#e5dec9]">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto">
    
    <!-- 2 Sections Side-by-Side in One Row (2 Columns) -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 lg:gap-8 items-stretch">
      
      <!-- Section 1: Why Business Development Executive? -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-8 lg:p-9 border border-[#ded5c5] shadow-xs flex flex-col justify-between hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
        <div>
          <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-[#eaf4ed] text-[#1c643b] text-xs font-semibold tracking-wider uppercase mb-3.5">
            <span>Core Role Spotlight</span>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-[#082213] tracking-tight mb-4">
            Why Business Development Executive?
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-3.5 text-xs sm:text-[13.5px] text-[#4d5e52] leading-relaxed font-normal">
            <p>
              A career as a <strong>Business Development Executive</strong> is more than just a job — it’s an opportunity to grow, learn, and lead. This role plays a crucial part in expanding the company’s reach and building long-term client relationships.
            </p>
            <p>
              As a BDE, you will be responsible for identifying new business opportunities, connecting with potential clients, and contributing to the overall growth of the company. This role helps you develop essential skills such as communication, negotiation, strategic thinking, and problem-solving.
            </p>
            <p>
              Moreover, the experience gained in this position lays a strong foundation for future leadership roles. It allows you to understand market trends, customer behavior, and business strategies, making you a valuable asset in any organization.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Section 2: Future Growth and Career Opportunities -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-8 lg:p-9 border border-[#ded5c5] shadow-xs flex flex-col justify-between hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
        <div>
          <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-[#f4ede0] text-[#082213] text-xs font-semibold tracking-wider uppercase mb-3.5 border border-[#ded5c5]">
            <span>Career Progression</span>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-[#082213] tracking-tight mb-4">
            Future Growth and Career Opportunities
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-3.5 text-xs sm:text-[13.5px] text-[#4d5e52] leading-relaxed font-normal">
            <p>
              The role of a Business Development Executive offers immense growth potential. As you gain experience and achieve results, you can move into higher roles such as <strong>Business Development Manager</strong>, <strong>Sales Manager</strong>, or even leadership positions.
            </p>
            <p>
              This career path not only enhances your professional skills but also boosts your confidence and decision-making abilities. You will gain exposure to different industries, clients, and business models, which broadens your perspective and strengthens your expertise.
            </p>
            <p>
              With consistent performance and dedication, you can build a successful and rewarding career in business development. The opportunities are endless for those who are willing to learn, adapt, and grow.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

  </div>
</section>
